# Database rules

Before a schema or data change:
- inspect existing schema and data assumptions;
- identify compatibility impact;
- consider production data volume;
- identify lock/downtime risk;
- consider rollback or roll-forward strategy;
- preserve integrity with appropriate constraints;
- review indexes for changed query patterns;
- use transactions when atomicity matters;
- avoid destructive migrations without an explicit migration strategy.

Never treat a schema change as isolated from existing data.
